    "description": "<p>An invisible cone of terror causes living creatures to become panicked. They suffer a \u20132 morale penalty on saving throws, and they flee from the caster. A panicked creature has a 50% chance to drop what it\u2019s holding, chooses its path randomly (as long as it is getting away from immediate danger), and flees any other dangers that confront it. If cornered, a panicked creature cowers. A cowering creature loses its Dexterity bonus, can take no actions, and takes a \u20132 penalty to its Defense.</p>",
